$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for Suzuki coupling reaction
of intermediate 22. To a vial containing corresponding boronic acid (0.5
mmol) was charged a stock solution of
(R)-2'-bromo-7'-(neopentyloxy)-5H-spiro[oxazole-4,9'-xanthen]-2-amine
(22) (0.050 g, 0.120 mmol), tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0)
(0.014 g, 0.012 mmol), and dioxane (1.5 mL). A solution of potassium
carbonate (0.095 g, 0.688 mmol) and water (0.6 mL) was added. The
reaction was stirred overnight at 100°C. The mixture was diluted with
DMSO and filtered through a syringe filter, which was flushed with
additional DMSO. The material was purified via HPLC (10-90% MeCN:H2O w/
0.1% TFA of formic acid modifier) or chromatography on silica gel to
afford corresponding products as corresponding salts or free bases.
(S)-2'-(5-methoxypyridin-3-yl)-7'-(neopentyloxy)-5H-spiro[oxazole-4,9'-xanthen]-2-amine
2,2,2-trifluoroacetate (30). Yield 77%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm
8.74 (br. s., 1 H), 8.39 (br. s., 1 H), 7.99 (s, 1 H), 7.78 (s, 1 H),
7.64 (d, J=8.8 Hz, 1 H), 7.34 (d, J=8.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.17 (d, J=9.1 Hz, 1
H), 7.02 (d, J=9.2 Hz, 1 H), 6.91 (br. s., 1 H), 4.82 (s, 2 H), 4.05 (s,
3 H), 3.54 -3.69 (m, 2 H), 1.06 (s, 9 H). MS m/z = 446.0 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Suzuki coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Lead Optimization and Modulation of hERG Activity in a Series of
Aminooxazoline Xanthene β-Site Amyloid Precursor Protein Cleaving Enzyme
(BACE1) Inhibitors
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Epstein, Oleg; Bryan, Marian C.; Cheng, Alan C.; Derakhchan, Katayoun;
Dineen, Thomas A.; Hickman, Dean; Hua, Zihao; Human, Jason B.; Kreiman,
Charles; Marx, Isaac E.; Weiss, Matthew M.; Wahl, Robert C.; Wen, Paul
H.; Whittington, Douglas A.; Wood, Stephen; Zheng, Xiao Mei; Fremeau,
