$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5. Synthesis of pyrazoles 7a-h (Scheme 4) General procedure: In a glass
tube fitted with a Teflon screw seal, Pd(PPh3)4 (0.02 mmol), K3PO4 ( 0.60
mmol) and the selected boronic acid (0.22 mmol) were added to a solution
of 3-bromo-5-iodo-1-(4-methoxyphenyl)-1H-pyrazole (5) (0.20 mmol) in a
degassed mixture of DMF/H2O (4:1, 2 mL). The reactor was flushed with
argon and the reaction mixture was left to stir at 50°C for 3 h. The
second boronic acid (0.26 mmol) was then added and the reaction mixture
was heated to 80°C overnight. Water (20 mL) was added and the reaction
mixture was extracted twice with AcOEt (2 x 20 mL). The combined organic
layers were dried over MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by column chromatography (silica gel, appropriate mixture of
cyclohexane/AcOEt) to afford the corresponding 3,5-disubstituted
pyrazole. 3-[1-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-5-thiophen-2-yl-1H-pyrazol-3-yl]pyridine
(7a): 54% yield, white solid, Mp:150-153°C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ.
3.86 (s, 3H), 6.87-7.97 (m, 5H), 7.27-7.38 (m, 4H), 8.19 (d, J = 7.9 Hz,
1H), 8.58 (br. s, 1H), 9.10 (br. s, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ.
55.7, 104.2, 114.5, 126.8, 127.4, 127.5, 127.9, 131.1, 132.8, 133.1,
139.1, 147.3, 148.7, 149.1, 160.0. HRMS (El): M+, 333.0932; calcd. for
C19H15N3OS: 333.0936.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective (stage 1), Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Modular Sydnone Cycloaddition/Suzuki-Miyaura Cross-Coupling Strategy to
Unsymmetrical 3,5-Bis(hetero)aromatic Pyrazoles
