$DATUM Porphyrin boronic ester 6 (255 mg 2.4 equiv), 7 (63 mg 1 equiv),
Pd(PPh3)4 (12 mg, 0.1 equiv) and Cs2CO3 (130 mg, 4 equiv) were dried
under vacuum and then purged with argon. To this degassed toluene (10 mL)
was added and the mixture was stirred for 36 hours at 96 °C. After
cooling, water was added and the product was extracted with ethyl acetate
(3 × 10 mL). The organic layer was washed with saturated brine and dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was removed under vacuum and the
residue was purified by column chromatography (silica gel, DCM: hexane =
1:3) to give a red waxy solid product 8 (180 mg, 77%). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500
MHz) δ: 9.06-9.08 (m, 8H), 8.95 (s, 8H), 8.82 (d, J= 7.6 Hz, 2H), 8.76
(s, 2H), 8.12-8.22 (m, 14H), 7.82-7.84 (m, 7H), 7.56-7.61 (m, 2H), 7.43
(d, J= 8.2 Hz, 2H), 6.07 (s, 2H), 1.56 (s, 108H), 1.03 (s, 18H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 125 MHz), δ: 151.5, 151.4, 150.6, 150.5, 150.3, 148.6, 148.5,
148.48, 142.0, 141.9, 137.8, 136.7, 133.7, 132.6, 132.2, 132.1, 131.7,
130.4, 129.7, 129.6, 126.9, 125.1, 123.8, 122.9, 122.4, 121.7, 121.0,
120.8, 120.5, 118.9, 118.3, 35.07, 35.05, 34.7, 31.82, 31.78, 31.3. anal.
calcd for C159H173N9Zn2: C, 81.58; H, 7.45; N, 5.39; Zn, 5.59. found C
81.40, H 7.66, N 5.23. MS (MALDI-TOF): m/z = 2340.480 (M+H)+; calcd. for
C159H173N9Zn2: 2339.240.
