$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 6-Pyridin-4-ylquinazolin-2-amine (6):
6-Bromoquinazolin-2-amine (5, 200 mg, 0.89 mmol), 4-pyridinylboronic acid
(165 mg, 1.34 mmol, 1.5 equiv), and K2CO3 (370 mg, 2.68 mmol, 3.0 equiv)
in DME/H2O (5:1, 4 mL) were treated with Pd(Ph3P)4 (206 mg, 0.179 mmol,
20 mol %). The reaction was stirred at 90 °C for 12 h. The reaction was
quenched with 10% NaOH and extracted with EtOAc. The combined organics
were dried with NaCl (satd) and then Na2SO4 (s). The solvents were
removed under reduced pressure. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography utilizing an ISCO system (EtOAc-MeOH) to give the title
compound. From 6-bromo-7-chloroquinazolin-2-amine (89).
7-Chloro-6-(pyridin-4-yl)quinazolin-2-amine (92) as a solvent, yield 3.42
g, 77%. 1H NMR: 9.18 (s, 1H), 8.64-8.75 (m, 2H), 7.94 (s, 1H), 7.60 (s,
1H), 7.48-7.58 (m, 2H), 7.21 (s, 2H). LC-MS: m/z 257.
