$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
4-Amino-5-phenyl-7-(β-D-ribofuranosyl)-7H-pyrrolo[2,3-d]pyrimidine (6a).
An argon purged mixture of 7-iodotubercidin 7 (200 mg, 0.51 mmol),
phenylboronic acid (93 mg, 0.76 mmol), Na2CO3 (502 mg, 4.74 mmol),
Pd(OAc)2 (6.6 mg, 0.029 mmol), and TPPTS (42 mg, 0.07 mmol) in water/MeCN
(2:1, 3.6 mL) was stirred at 100 °C for 1 h. After cooling, the mixture
was neutralized by the addition of aqueous HCl (1M), volatiles were
removed in vacuo and the residue was purified by reverse phase
chromatography (0→100% MeOH in water).
4-Amino-7-(β-D-ribofuranosyl)-5-(thiophen-3-yl)-7H-pyrrolo[2,3-d]pyrimidine
(6i). Compound 6i was prepared as described for 6a from compound 7 and
thiophene-3-boronic acid; yield 77%; white-grey solid after
recrystallization from MeOH. mp 197 °C; [α]20D -58.7 (c 0.237, DMSO). UV
(MeOH): λmax (ε) 281 (12100). 1H NMR (600 MHz, DMSO-d6): 3.53 (ddd, 1H,
Jgem = 12.0, J5'b,OH = 6.1, J5',4' = 3.8, H-5'b); 3.62 (ddd, 1H, Jgem =
12.0, J5'a,OH = 4.9, J5'a,4' = 3.9, H-5'a); 3.90 (ddd, 1H, J4',5' = 3.9,
3.8, J4',3' = 3.0, H-4'); 4.09 (bddd, 1H, J3',2' = 4.2, J3,OH = 3.2,
J3',4' = 3.0, H-3'); 4.43 (bddd, 1H, J2',1' = 6.3, J2',OH = 5.1, J2',3' =
4.2, H-2'); 5.14 (bd, 1H, JOH,3' = 3.2, OH-3'); 5.21 (dd, 1H, JOH,5' =
6.1, 4.9, OH-5'); 5.34 (bd, 1H, JOH,2' = 5.1, OH-2'); 6.09 (d, 1H, J1',2'
= 6.3, H-1'); 6.21 (bs, 2H, NH2); 7.27 (dd, 1H, J4,5 = 4.9, J4,2 = 1.3,
H-4-thienyl); 7.52 (dd, 1H, J2,5 = 2.9, J2,4 = 1.3, H-2-thienyl); 7.55
(s, 1H, H-6); 7.72 (dd, 1H, J5,4 = 5.1, J5,2 = 2.9, H-5-thienyl); 8.13
(s, 1H, H-2). 13C NMR (151 MHz, DMSO-d6): 61.90 (CH2-5'); 70.84 (CH-3');
74.00 (CH-2'); 85.32 (CH-4'); 87.17 (CH-1'); 101.00 (C-4a); 111.19 (C-5);
121.29 (CH-6); 122.24 (CH-2-thienyl); 127.62 (CH-5-thienyl); 128.71
(CH-4-thienyl); 134.94 (C-3-thienyl); 150.79 (C-7a); 151.96 (CH-2);
