$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-(5-(Benzo[d]thiazol-6-yl)-2-chloropyridin-3-yl)-4-fluorobenzenesulfonamide
(9). To a microwave vial equipped with a magnetic stir bar was added
6-bromobenzo[d]thiazole (0.100 g, 0.467 mmol), compound 7 (0.212 g, 0.514
mmol), PdCl2(dppf)•CH2Cl2 (0.0191 g, 0.0234 mmol), Cs2CO3 (0.457 g, 1.40
mmol), THF (3 mL), and water (0.5 mL). The vial was capped and heated by
microwave for 10 min at 100 °C. The reaction mixture was diluted with
water (10 mL), DCM (10 mL), and satd NaCl (5 mL). The solution was
extracted with DCM (3 x 20 mL), and the combined extracts were dried
(Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was
recrystallized from 5:1 DCM/MeOH and Et2O. The crystallized material was
collected by filtration and washed with Et2O and dried under vacuum to
afford 9 as a tan crystalline solid (0.150 g, 77% yield).
N-(5-(Benzo[d]thiazol-6-yl)-2-chloropyridin-3-yl)-4-fluorobenzenesulfonamide
(9), yield (0.150 g, 77%). HRMS calculated for C18H11ClFN3O2S2 (M + H)
420.0037, found 420.0028. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ ppm 7.42 (t, J =
8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.77-7.89 (m, 3H), 8.08 (d, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 8.22 (d, J =
8.4 Hz, 1H), 8.55 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 1H), 8.63 (d, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 9.48 (s,
1H), 10.54 (br s, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, sealed microwave vial used
