$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure. To a screw-capped vial was added Pd(OAc)2 (6.0 mg,
0.025 mmol, 5 mol%), P(p-C6H4F)3 (16 mg, 0.05 mmol, 10 mol%), CsOH.H2O
(168 mg, 1.0 mmol, 2 eq), and boronate ester 1 (155 mg, 0.50 mmol, 1 eq).
The vial was sealed with a PTFE septum and then evacuated and backfilled
with N2 (this sequence was carried out three times to ensure complete
degassing of viscous liquids). Toluene (2 mL, anhydrous/degassed) was
added via syringe through the septum, followed by vigorous stirring and
addition of the aryl bromide (0.55 mmol, 1.1 eq) was added via syringe
[Note: Aryl bromides that were solids were added with the other reagents
prior to evacuation]. The sealed reaction vessel was heated to 80 °C in
an aluminum heating block for 16 h. At this time, the reaction was
allowed to cool to room temperature and was diluted with EtOAc. The
resulting heterogeneous mixture was filtered through a pad of Celite
(eluted with additional EtOAc) and the eluent was concentrated under
reduced pressure. The crude material was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (heptanes/ethyl acetate) to afford the
2-heteroaryl tetrahydropyridine products. The purified 2-heteroaryl
tetrahydropyridine was dissolved in EtOH (4 mL) followed by addition of
NH4CO2H (20 eq) and 10 wt % Pd/C (20 % relative to tetrahydropyridine). A
reflux condenser was attached and the reaction was heated to 65 °C for 16
h. At this time, the reaction was filtered through a thin pad of Celite
(eluted with additional EtOH), and all solvent removed under reduced
pressure. The residue was re-dissolved in a minimal amount of CH2Cl2, to
complete precipitation of excess NH4CO2H, followed by filtration through
Celite (eluted with additional CH2Cl2) and evaporation of all solvent to
afford the indicated α-heteroaryl piperidine products without additional
purification required (unless otherwise noted). Compound 3a, yield 77%.
IR (film): 2937, 1688, 1413, 1273, 1157 cm-1. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 8.44-8.36
(m, 2H), 7.42 (m, 1H), 7.17 (m, 1H), 5.36 (m, 1H), 3.96 (m, 1H), 2.63 (m,
1H), 2.18 (m, 1H), 1.83 (m, 1H), 1.60-1.40 (m, 3H), 1.36 (s, 9H),
1.33-1.23 (m, 1H); 13C{1H} NMR (CDCl3): δ 155.4, 148.4, 147.8, 136.0,
134.5, 123.4, 80.0, 51.6, 40.2, 28.4, 27.9, 25.3, 19.3. HRMS
(ESI/[M+Na]+) calcd. for C15H22N2O2Na: 285.1573. Found:285.1578.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed vessel used (1st stage), Suzuki cross-coupling (1st stage), crude
intermediate isolated, alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Expedient Synthesis of α-Heteroaryl Piperidines Using a Pd-Catalyzed
Suzuki Cross-Coupling-Reduction Sequence
