$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step 2.
Tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (0.47 g, 0.411 mmol),
pyridin-3-ylboronic acid (1.010 g, 8.22 mmol),
(R)-2-amino-7'-bromo-3'-fluoro-5H-spiro[oxazole-4,9'-xanthen]-2'-ol (1.5
g, 4.11 mmol), and sodium carbonate (2M solution) (6.16 mL, 12.32 mmol)
were combined in DMF (10 ml). The mixture was heated at 90° C for 6
hours, cooled to room temperature and extracted with ethyl acetate.
Organic layer was washed with water and brine and concentrated. The
residue was purified via silica gel column chromatography (RediSep 80 g
column) using 0-100 % 90/10/1 (DCM/MeOH/ammonia) in DCM.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Suzuki-Miyaura coupling reaction
