$DATUM 142-82-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A mixture of
5-Bromo-3-[5-(4-ethyl-piperazin-1-yl)-pyridin-2-ylamino]-1-methyl-1H-pyridin-
2-one (50 g, 128mmol), Bis(pinacolato) diboron (33g, 130mmol), Pd(OAc)2
(1.43g, 6.4mmol), X-Phos (5.0 g, 10.5mmol), KOAc (50 g, 512mmol), and
dioxane (500 mL) was stirred and degassed three times. The mixture was
heated at 100°C for 2 hours then cooled to 65°C. The slurry was filtered
through a pad of Celite (100 g). The cake was washed with 800 mL of
dioxane. The filtrate was distilled under vacuum to 400 mL. The residue
was heated to 65°C. Heptane (700 mL) was slowly added over 1 h. The
slurry was cooled to room temperature and further cooled in an ice bath
for 4 hours. The product was isolated by filtration and washed with a
mixed solution of heptane (300 mL) and dioxane (150 mL) that had been
pre-cooled to 0°C. The cake was dried overnight in a 70° C. vacuum oven.
The product, 1-ethyl-3-[S-( 4-methyl-piperazin-I-yl)-pyridin-2-ylamino
5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl- [1,3,2]dioxaborolan-2-yl)-IH-pyridin-2-one, was
obtained as a brown solid (43 g, 77% yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structure-Based Drug Design of RN486, a Potent and Selective Bruton's
Tyrosine Kinase (BTK) Inhibitor, for the Treatment of Rheumatoid
Arthritis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
