$DATUM (±)-Methyl
4-(2-amino-5-(5-(piperidin-1-ylmethyl)thiophen-2-yl)pyridin-3-yl)-2-(1-(2-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)ethoxy)benzoate
16f A suspension of 5-(piperidinomethyl)-2-thiopheneboronic acid pinacol
ester (110 mg, 0.36 mmol), bromide rac-14a (76 mg, 0.15 mmol), sodium
carbonate (33 mg, 0.31 mmol) and tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0)
(18 mg, 0.016 mmol) in DME/water (8/1, 1.35 mL) was heated to 110°C under
microwave irradiation for 1 h. The reaction was quenched with brine and
extracted with EtOAc. The combined organics were washed with brine, dried
(Na2SO4), concentrated and purified by Biotage column chromatography
(0-5% MeOH/DCM). Pyridine 16f (69 mg, 76%). HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
C32H33F3N3O3S (M + H) 596.2189, found 596.2172. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
8.29 (s, 1H), 7.92 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.87 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.67
(d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.57 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.40-7.35 (m, 2H), 7.07
(d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 6.98 (d, J = 3.4 Hz, 1H), 6.93 (s, 1H), 6.85 (d, J =
3.4 Hz, 1H), 5.86-5.83 (m, 1H), 4.41 (s, 2H), 3.99 (s, 3H), 3.69 (s, 2H),
2.47 (s, 4H), 1.74 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 3H), 1.65-1.58 (m, 4H), 1.49-1.42 (m,
2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (in stage 1), Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design of Potent and Selective Hybrid Inhibitors of the Mitotic Kinase
Nek2: Structure-Activity Relationship, Structural Biology, and Cellular
Activity
