$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: III. Experimental for the Suzuki-Miyaura
reaction of lithium triisopropylborates with aryl halides in THF/water.
An oven-dried screw cap test tube was charged with precatalyst 13 (3.0%)
and lithium triisopropylborate (0.375 mmol or 0.75 mmol). The test tube
was evacuated and backfilled with argon (this sequence was carried out
three times). The aryl halide (0.25 mmol) was added via syringe through
the septum (solid aryl halides were added with the borate), followed by
the addition oft THF (0.5 mL or 1.0 mL) and water (1.0 mL or 2.0 mL). The
reaction mixture was stirred in a preheated oil bath at 40 °C for 2 h.
The tube was taken out of the oil bath and water (20 mL) and NH4Cl aq.
sat. (0.4 mL) were then added. The mixture was extracted with EtOAc (3 x
20 mL). The combined organic phases were dried over MgSO4, filtered, and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude material so obtained was
purified via the Biotage Isolera Four (silica-packed 10 g snap column;
EtOAc/hexanes). 2-(furan-3-yl)benzoxazole (29). Following the general
procedure, a mixture of 2-Chlorobenzoxazole (29 μL, 38 mg, 0.25 mmol),
lithium triisopropyl 3-furanylborate (98 mg, 0.375 mmol), and 13 (3 mol%)
yielded the title compound in 35 mg (76% yield) as a colorless solid. Mp
107-108 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 8.23 (dd, J = 1.5, 0.7 Hz, 1H),
7.77-7.69 (m, 1H), 7.58-7.51 (m, 2H), 7.38-7.31 (m, 2H), 7.04 (dd, J =
1.9, 0.7 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 158.3, 150.2, 144.4, 144.3,
141.8, 125.0, 125.6, 119.7, 115.4, 110.4, 109.0. IR(neat, cm-1): 1651,
1592, 1530, 1455, 1311, 1240, 1161, 1068, 1003. Anal Calcd. for C11H7NO2:
C, 71.35; H, 3.81. Found: C, 71.25; H, 3.69. 1H and 13C NMR spectra
included.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A General Method for Suzuki-Miyaura Coupling Reactions Using Lithium
Triisopropyl Borates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Oberli, Matthias A.; Buchwald, Stephen L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
