$DATUM Compound 14: 14a: A mixture of compound 10 (309mg, 2.2equiv), compound 13
(150mg, 1equiv), Pd(PPh3)4 (24mg, 10%equiv), K2CO3 (140mg, 5equiv) in 50
ml THF (2 ml H2O) was stirred at 66°C for 18 h under nitrogen. After
cooling to room temperature, the reaction mixture was poured into water
and the product was extracted with diethyl ether. The solvent was
evaporated under reduced pressure, and the crude product was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether/CH2Cl2, 4:1) to
yield the yellow solid product (263mg, 76%). Compound 14. Yield 263mg,
76%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz, 298K): δ = 8.75 (s, 6H), 8.16 (s, 4H), 8.04
(t, 4H), 7.93 (s, 5H), 7.79-7.63 (m, 15H), 7.54 (t, 2H), 7.35 (t, 2H),
4.68 (d, 6H), 2.37 (s, 3H), 1.42-1.10 (m, 72H) , 0.78-0.70 (m, 18H); 13C
NMR (CDCl3, 150 MHz, 298K): δ = 139.6, 136.7, 135.5, 133.8, 133.4, 132.4,
130.8, 130.7, 129.5, 129.0, 128.3, 127.9, 126.9, 126.0, 125.9, 125.6,
124.9, 124.7, 121.0, 117.4, 115.7, 115.3, 50.4, 40.1, 31.8, 31.7, 30.0,
29.7, 29.5, 29.3, 26.5, 22.6, 14.1, 14.0, 1.1. MS (MALDI-TOF): m/z (M+)
=1717.2 (calcd for C128H137N3: 1717.5).
