$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 2: A mixture of 3-bromo-1-trityl-pyrazolo[3,4-b]pyridine (5.0 g,
11.35 mmol), bis(pinacolato)diboron (5.76 g, 22.70 mmol) and potassium
acetate (3.34 g, 34.05 mmol) in dry DMF (65 mL) was degassed (N2/Vacuum
cycles) and treated with
1-cyclopenta-1,4-dienyl-diphenylphosphanedichloropalladiumiron. DCM
(926.9 mg, 1.14 mmol). The mixture was degassed again and heated to 105
°C under nitrogen for 16 h. After this time, the mixture was cooled to
room temperature, diluted with EtOAc (200 mL) and filtered through
celite. The celite was washed with EtOAc (150 mL) and the filtrate washed
with water (2 x 200 mL). Brine was added to aid phase separation. The
aqueous phase was back extracted with EtOAc (2 x 100 mL). The combined
organic phases were washed with saturated brine (75 mL), dried (MgSO4),
filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The crude material was dissolved in
DCM (20 mL) and filtered through a plug of Florisil (200 mesh), eluting
with 30% EtOAc/petroleum ether. The filtrate was concentrated in vacuo
and the resulting suspension was diluted with petroleum ether (50 mL),
which resulted in the rapid formation of a precipitate. This was stirred
in an ice bath for 30 minutes and then filtered. The solid was washed
with petroleum ether and dried under vacuum to afford
3-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1-trityl-pyrazolo[5,4-b]pyridine.
Off-white solid (4.19 g, 75.7 %). 1H NMR (DMSO-d6) δ 1.34 (12H, s), 7.31
-7.13 (16H, m), 8.34 -8.14 (2H, m). MS m/z: 488.3 (M + H)+.
