$DATUM Step 1: To a reaction vial was added
2-(6-chloro-5-methylpyridin-3-yl)acetic acid SI-9 (185 mg, 1 mmol),
2-fluoropyridin-4-ylboronic acid SI-10 (220mg, 1.5 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (12
mg, 0.05 mmol), S-Phos (41 mg, 0.1 mmol) and K3PO4 (636 mg, 3 mmol) in 1
mL 2-butanol. The reaction was heated to 100°C and stirred for 2 hours.
The reaction was cooled down to room temperature and then diluted to
DMSO. The reaction was filtered and the filtrate was purified by
reversephase HPLC. 2-(2'-fluoro-3-methyl-2,4'-bipyridin-5-yl)acetic acid
SI-11 as white solid (276 mg, 76 %).
