$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
7-(2,3-O-Isopropylidene-5-O-tert-butyldimethylsilyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-4-phenyl-7H-pyrrolo[
2,3-d]pyrimidine (10d). An argon purged mixture of compound 8 (309 mg,
0.7 mmol), phenylboronic acid (128 mg, 1.05 mmol), K2CO3 (193 mg, 1.4
mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (41 mg, 0.035 mmol) in toluene (5 mL) was stirred at
100 °C for 5 h. The mixture was diluted with chloroform (20 mL) and
washed with aqueous NH4Cl (sat., 20 mL). The aqueous phase was
re-extracted with chloroform (2×5 mL) and the combined organic extracts
dried over MgSO4, concentrated in vacuo and the residue chromatographed
on silica (hexanes-AcOEt, 10:1→7:1) to afford 10d (320 mg, 95%) as a
colorless oil.
4-(1-tert-Butoxycarbonyl-1H-pyrrol-2-yl)-7-(2,3-O-isopropylidene-5-O-tert-butyldimethylsilyl-
β-D-ribofuranosyl)-7H-pyrrolo[2,3-d]pyrimidine (10k). Compound 10k was
prepared as described for 10d by coupling compound 8 (0.92 mmol) and
1-N-(Boc)- pyrrole-2-boronic acid, but dimethoxyethane/H2O (4:1, 5 mL)
was used as solvent instead of toluene. Column chromatography on silica
gel eluting with hexanes-AcOEt, 18:1→17:1 provided 10k as a redish foam.
Yield 76%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): 0.057 and 0.063 (2 × s, 2 × 3H,
CH3Si); 0.90 (s, 9H, (CH3)3CSi); 1.28 (s, 9H, (CH3)3CO); 1.40 and 1.66 (2
× q, 2 × 3H, J = 0.6, (CH3)2C); 3.79 (dd, 1H, J gem= 11.2, J 5´b,4´= 3.9,
H-5´b); 3.89 (dd, 1H, J gem= 11.2,J 5´a,4´ = 3.9, H-5´a); 4.33 (td, 1H, J
4´,5´ = 3.9,J 4´,3´ = 3.2, H-4´); 4.99 (ddd, 1H, J 3´,2´ = 6.5, J 3´,4´ =
3.2, J 3´,1´ = 0.4, H-3´); 5.13 (dd, 1H, J 2´,3´ = 6.5, J 2´,1´ = 2.9,
H-2´); 6.33 (dd, 1H, J 4,3 = 3.4, J 4,5 = 3.2, H-4-pyrrole); 6.44 (d, 1H,
J 1´,2´ = 2.9, H-1´); 6.56 (d, 1H, J 5,6 = 3.8, H-5); 6.67 (dd, 1H, J 3,4
= 3.4, J 3,5= 1.7, H-3-pyrrole); 7.46 (dd, 1H,J 5,4 = 3.2, J 5,3 = 1.7,
H-5-pyrrole); 7.49 (d, 1H, J 6,5 = 3.8, H-6); 8.88 (s, 1H, H-2). 13C NMR
(125.7 MHz, CDCl3): -5.47 and - 5.37 (CH3Si); 18.38 (SiC(CH3)3); 25.51
((CH3)2C); 25.91 ((CH3)3CSi); 27.37 ((CH3)2C); 27.41 ((CH3)3CO); 63.37
(CH2-5´); 80.94 (CH-3´); 84.07 (OC(CH3)3); 84.95 (CH-2´); 86.01 (CH-4´);
90.23 (CH-1´); 101.25 (CH-5); 110.94 (CH-4-pyrrole); 114.15 (C(CH3)2);
117.35 (C-4a); 117.80 (CH-3-pyrrole); 124.98 (CH-5-pyrrole); 126.39
(CH-6); 130.83 (C-2-pyrrole); 149.07 (CO); 150.93 (C-7a); 151.16 (CH-2);
152.05 (C-4). MS FAB, m/z (rel. %): 73 (100), 471 (15), 515 (25), 571
(30)[M+H]. HR MS (FAB): calcd for C29H43N4O6Si [M+H] 571.2952, found
571.2957.
